<div id="2026-11-12-healthkitchen-recipe-make-hardening" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-12 — Health Kitchen: "Mark made" deducts all-or-nothing, and counts containers not grams</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> <code>consume_recipe</code> now runs every deduction inside one <code>txn_do</code>. A line that fails (helper returns not-ok, dies, or the item is not on this site) throws and rolls the whole make back, and the reply reports <code>rolled_back =&gt; 1</code> with the failing line instead of a partial deduct. Lines with no numeric quantity, no stock row for the SKU, or no pantry table are still reported as skipped and do not abort the make. Batch counts are validated (whole number, 1..<code>HealthKitchen.max_recipe_batches</code>, default 10, bounded 1..1000). A recipe line in grams is converted to a fraction of the stocked unit using <code>inventory_items.net_weight_g</code>; a line in any other unit, or with no net weight set, is skipped rather than guessed.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> A failure halfway through the ingredient list left stock short for the first lines and untouched for the rest, so the shelf disagreed with the app and the reply claimed the make succeeded. Stock is counted in containers while recipes are written in grams.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Util/HealthKitchen.pm</code> (<code>consume_recipe</code>, <code>stock_units_for_line</code>, <code>valid_batches</code>, <code>max_batches</code>, <code>_deduct_inventory</code>, <code>_deduct_pantry</code>), <code>lib/Comserv/Model/Schema/Ency/Result/Accounting/InventoryItem.pm</code>. Needs schema-compare: <code>inventory_items.net_weight_g</code> (decimal 10,2, NULL = unknown). The container fraction is rounded to 3 decimals to match the stock columns (<code>decimal(12,3)</code>); formatting it at 4 decimals only in the reply made the reported amount differ from what the database stored, and a fraction that rounds to 0.000 is now reported as skipped instead of deducting nothing.</p>
</div>
